From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ouroboros420 <ouroboros420@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] input: wait for input instead of polling, and stop streaming
 idle Steam reports

Every evdev source polled its device every 2.5 ms whether or not there was
input (there is even a TODO to use epoll here), and every target ticked on a
fixed interval. The Steam Deck uhid target also bumped its frame counter and
sent Steam a fresh input report on every 4 ms tick, forever. With nobody
touching the device that is well over a thousand wakeups a second in
InputPlumber, plus 250 a second in whatever reads the hidraw node.

Sources: SourceInputDevice gains wait_fd(). The evdev gamepad and keyboard
sources return their device fd while their translator has no scheduled
events pending, and the source thread then blocks in poll(2) on that fd and
an eventfd instead of sleeping. Every SourceDeviceClient send signals the
eventfd, so commands (including the FF uploads that wait 200 ms for a reply)
are still handled right away. The wait is capped at 250 ms, and sources
without a fd keep the old timer.

Targets: TargetOutputDevice gains is_idle(), false by default, so targets
that do time-based work in poll() (mouse motion from stick velocity,
touchpad timestamps, streamed reports) behave exactly as before. Targets
that report idle drop to a 50 ms tick after a second without commands or
output events. Input still wakes the loop immediately through the command
channel, so only host-to-device traffic (rumble, feature reports) can wait
that long.

deck-uhid only sends a report when its state changed (write_event(),
clear_state()), when a reader opens the device, or as a 1 s keepalive, and
reports idle once that is done. The keyboard target has nothing to poll and
always reports idle.

nix gains its poll and event features; no new crates.
